#
# WHY ONLY `vroid-sample-b` REDDENS ON P1 TO P4. `facingSign('1')` is +1, so
# removing a `fwd *` factor is the identity on the two 1.0 bodies and changes
# nothing there. The 0.x family is the one that carries the sign, and it is also
# the one every offered look belongs to. A mutation that reddened all three
# families would mean the factor was doing something on a body where it should
# not.
#
# P5, P6 and P7 redden once rather than three times because their tests are not
# per-family: they read gestureOffsets and the table's own name list, and never
# touch a rig.
#
# WHAT IS NOT MUTATION-BACKED, and deliberately. The two `axis semantics` tests
# measure the rig rather than a defence in this diff: no line of the gesture
# table can be changed to make "a positive yaw turns her toward her own left"
# false. They are there because they carry the argument for the scope of the
# fix, and they would redden if a future family body broke the assumption the
# scope rests on.
#
# The unmutated file is green: 31 passed.
